+            "screened at the unchanged one-boundary nearest-baseline served guard, then all eligible "
+            "swaps were committed over 48 boundaries and compared by strict binary64 demand-capped "
+            "pooled user efficiency. These newly tested capped swaps are diagnostic only and are not "
+            "fed into the headroom tables.",
+            "",
+            "| rule/endpoint | legal pairs | eligible after physical validity + guard | F-improving swaps in source | demand-capped-improving swaps | not F-2-swap-optimal | not demand-capped-2-swap-optimal | best capped gain |",
+            "|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|",
+        ]
+    )
+    for anchor, endpoint, audit in audits:
+        best = audit["best_improving_swap"]
+        lines.append(
+            f"| `{anchor['rule']} {anchor['anchor']} start {endpoint['start_index']}` "
+            f"| {audit['legal_swap_pair_count']} | {audit['eligible_committed_swap_count']} "
+            f"| {audit['receipt_F_feasible_improving_swap_count']} "
+            f"| {audit['strictly_demand_capped_improving_swap_count']} "
+            f"| {'yes' if not audit['receipt_F_is_two_swap_optimal'] else 'no'} "
+            f"| {'yes' if not audit['is_demand_capped_two_swap_optimal'] else 'no'} "
+            f"| {'—' if best is None else signed_pct(best['relative_gain_over_endpoint'])} |"
+        )
+    lines.extend(
+        [
+            f"| **subset count** | — | — | — | — | **{f_nonoptimal}/2** | **{capped_nonoptimal}/2** | — |",
+            "",
+            "The original full-set statement remains a verified receipt fact—128/128 were not "
+            "2-swap optimal for one-boundary `F = B − eta_ref E`—but it is not evidence about the "
+            "reporting numerator. Only the predeclared 2-endpoint subset was fully retested under "
+            "demand-capped committed EE; a full 128-endpoint capped swap census was infeasible in the "
+            "available run budget and was not silently replaced by a proxy.",
+            "",
+            "## Derived on paper",
+            "",
+            "All pooled EEs above are `sum credited bits / sum joules`, never averages of anchor EEs. "
+            "`best found exceeds reference = EE_best / EE_ref − 1` (reference denominator). "
+            "`reference below best found = 1 − EE_ref / EE_best` (best-found denominator). Spreads are "
+            "`max/min − 1`. Cohort shares divide each signed raw-capacity cohort increment by their "
